  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Export incentives helped shape Jacques Bruynooghe’s manufacturing business. The Belgian entrepreneur used Tunisia’s export-promotion framework to build a supplier for international fashion companies. His factories made clothing for brands including Levi’s, H&M, Zara and Pimkie, linking local production to retailers serving customers far beyond Tunisia.\n\nHis business responsibilities extended to Belgium. At the clothing company Brunotex, he served as managing director and represented Jacques Bruynooghe Garments on its board. The group closed its five Tunisian subsidiaries in 2013. His corporate work continued beyond the textile group: he returned as a director and managing director of Classic Invest in 2023.",
    "html": "<p>Export incentives helped shape Jacques Bruynooghe’s manufacturing business. The Belgian entrepreneur used Tunisia’s export-promotion framework to build a supplier for international fashion companies. His factories made clothing for brands including Levi’s, H&amp;M, Zara and Pimkie, linking local production to retailers serving customers far beyond Tunisia.</p>\r\n<p>His business responsibilities extended to Belgium. At the clothing company Brunotex, he served as managing director and represented Jacques Bruynooghe Garments on its board. The group closed its five Tunisian subsidiaries in 2013. His corporate work continued beyond the textile group: he returned as a director and managing director of Classic Invest in 2023.</p>\r\n",
